cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HCRD, please cite this software release and the accompanying manuscript."
title: "HCRD: Reference Implementation and Reproducibility Archive"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Baturin
    given-names: Saveliy
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    email: saveliy.xo@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Safreliy/hcrd"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and reproducibility archive for Hierarchical
  Convexity-Run Decomposition (HCRD), a nonlinear geometric multiscale
  representation of sampled curves. The archive includes tests, experimental
  protocols, compact outputs, and materials supporting finite-sample recovery
  results and downstream validation studies.
keywords:
  - signal decomposition
  - discrete curvature
  - convexity
  - transient morphology
  - persistence
  - LC-MS
  - chromatographic quality control
  - interpretable signal representation
